From: Mark Kim <39310405+mk-imagine@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Apr 2026 21:27:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 060/110] daemon: add boot and deacon idle guards (#3519)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* daemon: skip Boot spawn when Deacon is healthy and no work is active

Boot spawns a full Claude Code session every ~2 min even with no work
queued and a healthy Deacon, burning AI tokens continuously. Add an idle
guard: skip Boot spawn when deacon.ReadHeartbeat().IsFresh() and no beads
are in_progress or hooked. Conservative fallbacks ensure Boot still runs
when stores are unavailable, queries fail, or no heartbeat exists.

Mirrors the existing refinery event-gate pattern (commit 3343b05d).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

* daemon: skip Deacon nudge when no active work is in flight

When the Deacon's heartbeat goes stale during an await-signal backoff
sleep, checkDeaconHeartbeat() was sending a nudge unconditionally. This
interrupts the Deacon's exponential backoff (max 15 min) for no reason —
the Deacon will wake naturally at its next timeout.

Add an idle guard: suppress the nudge when no in_progress or hooked beads
exist in any store. Mirrors the Boot idle guard (ensureBootRunning) and
the precedent in runtime/runtime.go where a session-started nudge was
removed for the same reason.

Conservative: hasActiveWork returns true on store error or empty stores,
so the nudge fires in any uncertain state.

* daemon: exclude hooked beads from hasActiveWork idle check

Patrol agent wisps (mol-deacon-patrol, mol-witness-patrol,
mol-refinery-patrol) are always in hooked state while agents run
their formula cycles. This caused hasActiveWork() to always return
true, preventing the Boot and Deacon idle guards from ever firing.

Fix: query only in_progress beads. The hooked status is used by
patrol formula epics, not by polecat work that Boot triage would
meaningfully address. A bead in hooked state is waiting on a hook
callback — not a stuck situation Boot can resolve.

Confirmed live on namu-sorim: Boot spawn skipped log message
appears on first heartbeat cycle after idle guard now triggers
correctly.

* docs: move research notes to docs/fork-info and gitignore

Renames docs/research/ → docs/fork-info/ (tracked separately, not
committed to this branch). Adds docs/fork-info/ to .gitignore so
private fork planning notes stay out of upstream PR diffs.

* chore: normalize CRLF to LF in molecule_await/emit_event files

